    "title": "Mizzou vs. Miami Hurricanes basketball TV channel, stream, game time",
    "text": "Anthony Robinson II #0 of the Missouri Tigers dribbles against the Kentucky Wildcats during the first half in the second round of the 2026 SEC Men's Basketball Tournament at Bridgestone Arena on March 12, 2026, in Nashville, Tennessee. Carly Mackler/Getty ImagesThe Missouri and Miami Hurricanes men's basketball teams are scheduled to meet in the 2026 March Madness NCAA Tournament first round at the Enterprise Center in St. Louis on Friday, March 20. The game is scheduled to start at 10:10 p.m. ET/9:10 p.m. CT.Article continues below this adMissouri enters the NCAA Tournament at 20-12 overall. Most recently, Kentucky beat Mizzou 78-72 in the SEC Tournament second round. Against Kentucky, Missouri forward Mark Mitchell led the team with 32 points and seven rebounds. The Miami Hurricanes come into the NCAA Tournament at 25-8 overall. On Friday, Virginia defeated the Miami Hurricanes 84-62 in the ACC Tournament semifinals. Facing Virginia, Miami Hurricanes guard Tru Washington led the team with 13 points and two steals. March Madness: How to watch Mizzou vs. Miami Hurricanes basketball on TV, live stream Jayden Stone #17 of the Missouri Tigers dribbles against the Kentucky Wildcats during the first half in the second round of the 2026 SEC Men's Basketball Tournament at Bridgestone Arena on March 12, 2026, in Nashville, Tennessee.Carly Mackler/Getty ImagesGame time: 10:10 p.m. ET/9:10 p.m. CT on Friday, March 20Article continues below this adTV channel: truTVtruTV broadcasters are scheduled to be Spero Dedes (play-by-play), Jim Spanarkel (analyst), and Jon Rothstein (reporter). On DirecTV, truTV is channel 246. On Dish, truTV is channel 242.Article continues below this adOnline live stream: HBOmax.comOnline radio broadcast: Varsity Network app and TheVarsityNetwork.comTerrestrial radio broadcasts: KTGR-AM 1580 (Columbia, Missouri); KTGR-FM 100.5 (Columbia, Missouri); KTRS-AM 550 (St. Louis) Article continues below this adDennis Gates is the Missouri men's basketball head coach. Jai Lucas is the Miami Hurricanes men's basketball head coach. T.O. Barrett #5 of the Missouri Tigers warms up prior to the second round of the 2026 SEC Men's Basketball Tournament against the Kentucky Wildcats at Bridgestone Arena on March 12, 2026, in Nashville, Tennessee.Carly Mackler/Getty ImagesDon't miss news and stories you need to read.March 19, 2026Erik Hall is the managing editor of The Telegraph. He was named the 2017 LGBTQ+ Journalist of the Year by NLGJA: The Association of LGBTQ+ Journalists. He holds a bachelor's degree in journalism from the University of Illinois and a master's degree in journalism from the University of Missouri.",
